## ID namespaces

`nav.*`, `search.query`, `sidebar.filters.*`, `sidebar.categories.*`, `sidebar.stats.*`, `home.*`, `category.*`, `thread.*` (incl. `thread.reply.*` and `thread.replies.*`), `new-thread.*`, `login.*`, `register.*`, `profile.*`, `not-found.*`.

## Collections — all fold

Verified in a real browser (built app, Playwright) rather than only in source: `sidebar.filters` (3), `sidebar.categories` (6), `home.threads` (8), `category.threads`, `thread.replies`, `profile.interests` (4), `profile.threads`. Every `.item.` id resolves to a `role="collection"` ancestor on every screen, logged in and out. **Nothing failed to fold.**

Two uniqueness hazards handled per §8: `ThreadCard` takes a required `semtagCollection` prop so the same thread in `home.threads`, `category.threads` and `profile.threads` gets a scoped id; interest tags are slugified (`"Open Source"` → `open-source`) so ids stay addressable.

